// AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/generate_poll_shared.py -- do not hand-edit.
// The single shared 'brain' script every area trampoline calls via
// ExecuteScript("ap_poll_shared", OBJECT_SELF). Editing/recompiling THIS
// file is the only redevelopment cost for new checks -- the 97 area
// trampolines that call it never need to change.
#include "kse"

// Area-visited checks are done INLINE in each area trampoline, not here --
// a global set immediately before ExecuteScript was confirmed NOT visible
// to the called script in this engine build (true for both string and
// number globals). See generate_area_trampolines.py for the area-check
// logic and PHASE10 notes for the full writeup.

// NOTE: custom (non-globalcat.2da) global variable names were confirmed
// this session to NOT persist in this engine build -- SetGlobalBoolean/
// SetGlobalNumber on any made-up name silently fails to stick, even
// same-tick in the cleanest possible test. So none of the checks below
// use custom globals for dedup/seen-tracking any more -- they report
// UNCONDITIONALLY every poll whenever the real, engine-native condition
// (a real globalcat.2da quest flag, IsAvailableCreature, current XP) is
// true. Deduplication now lives on the extender/AP-client side, which has
// real, uncapped persistent storage -- not in the game scripts.
